31. Amending Article 36 of the said Law as follows.

Registration of places other than schools that provide teaching
36. (a) Places other than schools that provide teaching shall be operated in the Maldives only after [?] registration in accordance with the principles set out in the regulation made under this Law.

(b) For the purpose of (a) of this Article, the following places shall be considered places other than schools that provide teaching.

[stamp] [signature]

(1) Baby nurseries and nurseries, and places of that level operated for the purpose of daycare education;

(2) Places that give tuition;

(3) Quran classes;

(4) Other places providing teaching specified in the regulation made under this Law.

(c) Applications to register the places specified in (a) of this Article shall be submitted to the Ministry. And the Ministry shall make the regulations that need to be made under this Law in relation to registering those places, monitor [?] the operation of those places, and take the necessary actions.

(d) The regulation formulated by the Ministry under (a) of this Article in relation to places providing teaching shall include at least the following matters.

(1) The conditions for registering places providing teaching;

(2) Registering places providing teaching and the manner in which they shall be operated, the information and documents that must be completed in that operation, and the principles and procedures the Ministry follows in relation to registration;

(3) The facilities and services that must be in place at places providing teaching;

(4) The principles for admitting children to and removing children from places providing teaching;

(5) The principles for determining the age of children admitted to places providing teaching;

[stamp] [signature]

the principle specified in (a), (b) and (c) of this Article shall also apply to them.

(e) For the purpose of this Article, the meaning of teachers includes teachers teaching in the places specified in (b) and (c) of this Article, teachers, leading teachers of the school, heads of departments, head teachers, technical staff working in posts of that level, deputy principals, acting principals, principals, and technical staff working in posts of that level.

(f) The regulations and principles for registering teachers in the Maldives and issuing licences to teachers under this Article shall be determined in the regulation made under this Law. Accordingly, the regulation formulated shall include at least the following matters. And the manner in which applications for registration and/or a licence must be submitted, the information and documents that must be completed in that application, and the principles and procedures followed in relation to registration shall be set out in that regulation.

(1) The conditions and principles of registration;

(2) The types, conditions and gradings of teaching licences;

(3) The manner in which applications for registration of teachers and/or for a teaching licence must be submitted, the information and documents that must be completed in that application, and the principles and procedures to be followed in relation to registration and issuing licences;

